    <briefdescription>
<para>Bounds the absolute value of a particle&apos;s stiffness times nonnegative weights, <formula id="71">$ |\boldsymbol{K}|\, \boldsymbol{W} $</formula>, from the stiffness it describes node by node, without forming it. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>What a critical time step needs from a stiffness is a bound of its spectral radius, e.g. the Collatz-Wielandt bound, <formula id="201">$ \max_i (|\boldsymbol{K}|\boldsymbol{w})_i / w_i $</formula> for positive weights <formula id="202">$ \boldsymbol{w} $</formula>. The stiffness of a particle with <formula id="82">$ n $</formula> nodes has <formula id="165">$ n^2 $</formula> blocks; this bound of <formula id="203">$ |\boldsymbol{K}|\boldsymbol{W} $</formula> costs <formula id="204">$ O(n) $</formula>: the rows of node <formula id="16">$ A $</formula> are linear in the shape functions of the other node <formula id="163">$ B $</formula> (see <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_meshfree_1_1_stiffness_visitor" kindref="compound">StiffnessVisitor</ref>), and the sum over <formula id="163">$ B $</formula> is taken from a few weighted moments of the shape functions, computed once per particle (<ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_meshfree_1_1_absolute_stiffness_bound_1a82f1d4575f5bbebaffe338326a9aa1fe" kindref="member">visitShapeFunctions()</ref>). Row <formula id="15">$ i $</formula> of node <formula id="16">$ A $</formula>, column component <formula id="99">$ k $</formula>, with the weights <formula id="205">$ w_B $</formula> of component <formula id="99">$ k $</formula> of the nodes and the factors <formula id="206">$ a = \partial f_{Ai}/\partial \Delta q_k $</formula>, <formula id="207">$ \boldsymbol{b} $</formula> (its gradient factors) and <formula id="208">$ \boldsymbol{h} $</formula> (its second-gradient factors):      <formula id="209">\[  \sum_B |K_{Ai,Bk}|\, w_B \le |a| \sum_B w_B |N_B|
  + \sqrt{ \sum_B w_B \|\boldsymbol{g}_B\| \; \boldsymbol{b}^T \Big( \sum_B
    \frac{w_B}{\|\boldsymbol{g}_B\|} \boldsymbol{g}_B \boldsymbol{g}_B^T \Big) \boldsymbol{b} }
  + (\text{the same for } \boldsymbol{h} \text{ and the second gradients}),
\]</formula> with <formula id="210">$ \boldsymbol{g}_B = \partial N_B / \partial \boldsymbol{Y} $</formula>. The first term is exact; the others are the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality over the nodes,   <formula id="211">$ \sum_B w_B |\boldsymbol{b}\cdot\boldsymbol{g}_B| \le
\sqrt{\sum_B w_B \|\boldsymbol{g}_B\|} \sqrt{\sum_B w_B (\boldsymbol{b}\cdot\boldsymbol{g}_B)^2 /
\|\boldsymbol{g}_B\|} $</formula>, which keeps the directions of the gradients: it is exact if all gradients are parallel, and <formula id="212">$ 2/\sqrt{3} $</formula> times the exact sum ( <formula id="213">$ \pi/(2\sqrt{2}) $</formula> in 2D) if their directions are spread evenly. The terms are added by the triangle inequality. The bound holds for every stiffness of the form of <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_meshfree_1_1_stiffness_visitor" kindref="compound">StiffnessVisitor</ref>, symmetric or not; the second gradients of the shape functions must be symmetric (their symmetric components are used).</para>
<para>A host uses it through <ref refid="_marmot_particle_stiffness_visitors_8h_1a3d65119bd6c2ee382e8727acb4941ebe" kindref="member">addBoundOfAbsoluteStiffnessTimes()</ref>.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>nDim</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Spatial dimension. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
